.SH "نام (NAME)"
arch-nspawn \- Run a command or OS in a light\-weight namespace container
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
arch\-nspawn [options] working\-dir [systemd\-nspawn arguments]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fIarch\-nspawn\fP is a wrapper around systemd\-nspawn to run command or OS in a
namespace container such as a directory including base utilities of a OS.
It is used to build package(s) in given clean and defined environment.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.sp
\fB\-C\fP <file>
.RS 4
Location of a pacman config file
.RE
.sp
\fB\-M\fP <file>
.RS 4
Location of a makepkg config file. Specific additions (e.g. build flags for
additional languages) can be placed in \fI<file>.d/*.conf\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-c\fP <dir>
.RS 4
Set pacman cache, if no directory is specified the passed pacman.conf\(cqs cachedir is used with a fallback to \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fP
.RE
.sp
\fB\-f\fP <src>[:<dst>]
.RS 4
Copy file from the host to the chroot.
If \fIdst\fP is not provided, it defaults to \fIsrc\fP inside of the chroot.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-s\fP
.RS 4
Do not run setarch
.RE
.sp
\fB\-h\fP
.RS 4
Show this usage message
.RE
.SH "HOMEPAGE"
.sp
\fI\c
.URL "https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/devtools" "" "\fP"
.sp
Please report bugs and feature requests in the issue tracker. Please do your best to provide a reproducible test case for bugs.